                                    <h1>Why We Chose to Be a Tech + Marketing Studio, Not Just One — By Prashant Chaudhari</h1>
                                    <p>A common piece of advice for services companies is 'specialise or die.' I've deliberately not followed it at ITD GrowthLabs. We built a combined tech + marketing studio — engineering and growth under one roof — because we believe the market is moving toward companies that need both, not one specialist plus a second specialist. Here is why we made the call and what it has cost + unlocked.</p>
                                    <h2>The Conventional Wisdom</h2>
                                    <p>Specialise. Own a category. Be famous for one thing. Every services book, every VC deck, every startup thesis says this. And it's true for many businesses. But it's also increasingly wrong for a growing category of client — modern D2C and B2B tech companies that need engineering and marketing so tightly integrated that treating them as separate purchases produces friction, waste, and slower outcomes.</p>
                                    <h2>Why the Traditional Specialisation Model Breaks</h2>
                                    <p>Marketing depends on engineering — page speed, structured data, indexation, tracking, personalisation, CRO infrastructure. Engineering depends on marketing — which features matter, which segments to build for, which retention signals to instrument. When these live in different companies, information gets lost. Decisions get delayed. Handoffs create defects. Founders spend management energy triangulating between vendors instead of building.</p>
                                    <h2>The Integrated Play</h2>
                                    <p>At ITD GrowthLabs, marketing and engineering are literally the same practice. Every engagement is jointly owned by an engineering lead and a marketing lead. Landing pages are engineered with SEO, performance, analytics, and schema baked in. Marketing campaigns are built with engineering visibility so infrastructure implications get handled upfront. Retention flows are treated as engineering deliverables, not marketing wireframes.</p>
                                    <h2>What This Has Cost Us</h2>
                                    <p><strong>Positioning complexity.</strong> Explaining what we do takes longer. Two-word descriptions ('digital marketing agency' or 'dev shop') don't apply.<br><strong>Talent recruitment.</strong> We can't post 'senior marketer' or 'senior engineer' — we need people who understand both, or specialists willing to operate in an integrated environment.<br><strong>Awards + industry recognition.</strong> Awards are organised by category (best agency, best dev shop). We fit neither cleanly.<br><strong>Analyst coverage.</strong> Analysts categorise by specialty; integrated firms confuse them.</p>
                                    <h2>What This Has Unlocked</h2>
                                    <p><strong>Deeper client relationships.</strong> When we're the strategic partner for both tech and growth, we see the full picture. Clients stop bouncing decisions between vendors.<br><strong>Compounding learnings.</strong> Marketing insights inform engineering priorities and vice versa within the same team.<br><strong>Faster shipping.</strong> A landing page that takes months at split-vendor companies ships in a week at ours.<br><strong>Higher-value engagements.</strong> Multi-year strategic engagements price 2-4x higher than pure execution.</p>
                                    <h2>Who This Model Fits Best</h2>
                                    <p>D2C brands ₹10-100 Cr ARR. Growth-stage B2B tech companies. Enterprises launching new digital business lines. Any company where the split between 'the product' and 'how customers hear about the product' is artificial. Companies that need one thing (pure marketing, pure engineering, pure design) are usually better served by specialists.</p>
                                    <h2>Why I Still Believe This Is the Right Call</h2>
                                    <p>Because the market is moving this way. Every year, more D2C and B2B companies realise that separated marketing + engineering vendors are slowing them down. Companies that offer integrated capability with senior-heavy teams and outcome pricing will keep growing faster than specialists over the next decade. That's what we're building.</p>

                                    <div style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a1a2e 0%, #16213e 100%); padding: 40px; border-radius: 12px; margin: 40px 0; text-align: center; color: #fff;">
                                        <h3 style="color:#fff;margin-bottom:15px;">Ready to Get Started?</h3>
                                        <p style="color:#ccc;margin-bottom:25px;">If your company is at the point where marketing and engineering silos are slowing you down, book a 30-minute call with me to talk about whether an integrated model would help.</p>
                                        <a href="https://www.itdgrowthlabs.com/contact-us.php" style="background:#ff5722;color:#fff;padding:14px 32px;border-radius:6px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;display:inline-block;margin-right:10px;">Contact Us Today</a>
