                                    </div>

                                    <div class="faq-section" style="margin-top:40px;">
                                        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
                                        <h3>Isn't specialisation always safer?</h3>
                                        <p>For most services companies, yes. For companies serving clients whose problem inherently spans marketing and engineering, integration wins.</p>
                                        <h3>Can one firm really be excellent at both?</h3>
                                        <p>Yes, with deliberate team composition. Senior generalists at leadership level, specialists at execution level, shared operating model.</p>
                                        <h3>What kind of client is best fit?</h3>
                                        <p>D2C brands and growth-stage B2B tech companies where product + growth are inseparable. Pure enterprise engineering or pure brand campaigns fit specialists better.</p>
                                        <h3>Are you worried about being categorised in future?</h3>
                                        <p>Some. But the market shift toward integrated capability is real. Being early to the model has costs but the pay-off is compounding.</p>
